  "question_stem": "Two particles $P$ and $Q$, of masses $0.3\\text{ kg}$ and $0.2\\text{ kg}$ respectively, are attached to the ends of a light inextensible string. The string passes over a fixed smooth pulley at $B$ which is attached to two inclined planes. $P$ lies on a smooth plane $AB$ which is inclined at $60^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal. $Q$ lies on a plane $BC$ which is inclined at $30^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal. The string is taut and the particles can move on lines of greatest slope of the two planes (see diagram).\n",
